## 7. Standard Operating Procedure (SOP)

## 7.1 Gold Image Initialization

The environment should be initialized in the master image or build pipeline before the desktop image is sealed and distributed. This ensures that OneDrive is installed as a machine-level component and that policy defaults are already aligned.

### PowerShell: Machine-Level Installation

```powershell
<#
.SYNOPSIS
    SOP Step: Automated OneDrive installation at the machine level
#>

$ErrorActionPreference = "Stop"

# Stop active runtime instances
Stop-Process -Name "OneDrive" -Force -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue

# Remove legacy per-user installation if present
$UserSetup = "$env:LocalAppData\Microsoft\OneDrive\OneDriveSetup.exe"
if (Test-Path $UserSetup) {
    Start-Process -FilePath $UserSetup -ArgumentList "/uninstall" -Wait -NoNewWindow
}

# Download the approved corporate package from the internal distribution point
$InstallerPath = "$env:TEMP\OneDriveSetup.exe"
Invoke-WebRequest -Uri "https://your-internal-distribution.example/OneDriveSetup.exe" -OutFile $InstallerPath

# Install for all users
$InstallResult = Start-Process -FilePath $InstallerPath -ArgumentList "/allusers", "/silent" -Wait -PassThru
if ($InstallResult.ExitCode -ne 0) {
    throw "OneDrive installation failed with exit code $($InstallResult.ExitCode)"
}
```

### Expected Outcome

The runtime should be installed under the system-level path:

```text
C:\Program Files\Microsoft OneDrive\
```

rather than under the local user profile.

> [!NOTE]
> Use an approved internal distribution source only. Do not deploy from arbitrary public URLs or unsecured download paths.

