## 7.3 Group Policy Deployment

The following GPO patterns provide a practical model for enterprise deployment.

### GPO 1: VMware VDI – Development and Quality Assurance

Objective: maintain user productivity while reducing uncontrolled profile growth.

Recommended settings:

- Computer Configuration > Administrative Templates > System > Group Policy
  - Configure user Group Policy loopback processing mode: Enabled (Replace)

- Computer Configuration > Administrative Templates > Windows Components > OneDrive
  - Use OneDrive Files On-Demand: Enabled
  - Prevent users from turning off Files On-Demand: Disabled

- Computer Configuration > Administrative Templates > System > Storage Sense
  - Allow Storage Sense: Enabled
  - Configure Storage Sense cloud content dehydration: Enabled (30 days)

This is a balanced policy set for users whose workflows may require access to large local content during software development or validation.

### GPO 2: Azure Hybrid VMs – Consultants and Restricted Users

Objective: minimize local persistence, reduce footprint, and enforce stricter security boundaries.

Recommended settings:

- Computer Configuration > Administrative Templates > System > Group Policy
  - Configure user Group Policy loopback processing mode: Enabled (Replace)

- Computer Configuration > Administrative Templates > Windows Components > OneDrive
  - Use OneDrive Files On-Demand: Enabled
  - Prevent users from turning off Files On-Demand: Enabled
  - Block syncing personal OneDrive accounts: Enabled

- Computer Configuration > Administrative Templates > System > Storage Sense
  - Allow Storage Sense: Enabled
  - Configure Storage Sense cloud content dehydration: Enabled (3 days)

- User Configuration > Administrative Templates > Windows Components > OneDrive
  - Silently sign in users to OneDrive with their Windows credentials: Enabled

This policy set is appropriate for high-risk or tightly controlled user classes where footprint and governance matter more than local file availability.

> [!CAUTION]
> A single policy baseline should not be used for every user group. Developer, business, and consultant environments have different operational risk profiles.

